  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Creating the first safe and sustainable pork value chain of Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: This project has been cancelled, because of the outbreak of African Swine Flue in Vietnam.In Vietnam, food safety is a major issue. There is a lack of production standards and tracking and tracing mechanisms for food. This also counts for pork meat. Pork consumption accounts for 70% of total meat in Vietnam and the strategic plan of the livestock production sector towards 2020 is to increase livestock production and to improve productivity and quality of pork to meet the local demand. It is currently difficult to get farmers producing meat of higher quality because the margins on hogs are really low.Currently, it is difficult to get farmers producing meat of higher quality because the margins on hogs are really low. The project aims to set up a certified chain for safe pork meat and realise a market with a higher market price for safe pork meat. The project will use high quality inputs and raise pigs in a suitable well monitored environment. Every step of the chain will be independently audited and certified. Traceability is assured according to international standards.Through this project farmers will get the chance to gain a better margin on their pigs because the joint venture will create a new market with higher prices for this quality meat.The partners will realise this by:&#x2022;	setting up a demonstration farm to a) show farmers different aspects of modern safe pig farming.&#x2022;	producing the first safe piglets as first part of the safe chain.&#x2022;	training farmers and have them let the piglets fattening into hogs and help them get certified for Viet Gap.&#x2022;	setting up a sales and trade department for selling the higher quality pork meat at a higher market price to the supermarkets.The project will be realised close to HCMC. The demonstration farm and offices will be totally 3,600 m2.The project will be realised by applicant De Heus Animal Nutrition B.V. and Fresh Studio Innovations Asia Ltd. They will set up a joint venture.</narrative>
  </description>
